**[Original report](https://bitbucket.org/mrabarnett/mrab-regex/issue/395) by animalize (Bitbucket: [animalize](https://bitbucket.org/animalize), GitHub: [animalize](https://github.com/animalize)).**

----------------------------------------

Python’s re module uses macro to produce different code for `Py_UCS1`/`Py_UCS2`/`Py_UCS4`

regex module uses `switch (state->charsize)` to process different `str` kinds. This is inefficient a bit, and makes the machine code segment fatter \(not cache friendly?\).

If move the related code to `regex_lib.h`, and include it in `_regex.c`, like re module, then `switch (state->charsize)` can be eliminated.

For example, in `regex_lib.h`:

```c
/* Matches many ANYs, up to a limit. */
Py_LOCAL_INLINE(Py_ssize_t)
SRE(match_many_ANY)(RE_State* state, RE_Node* node,
                    Py_ssize_t text_pos, Py_ssize_t limit, BOOL match) {
    void* text;
    SRE_CHAR* text_ptr;
    SRE_CHAR* limit_ptr;

    text = state->text;

    text_ptr = (SRE_CHAR*)text + text_pos;
    limit_ptr = (SRE_CHAR*)text + limit;

    while (text_ptr < limit_ptr && (text_ptr[0] != '\n') == match)
        ++text_ptr;

    text_pos = text_ptr - (SRE_CHAR*)text;

    return text_pos;
}
```

In `_regex.c`:

```c
/* generate 8-bit version */
#define SRE_CHAR Py_UCS1
#define SIZEOF_SRE_CHAR 1
#define SRE(F) sre_ucs1_##F
#include "regex_lib.h"
#undef SRE_CHAR
#undef SIZEOF_SRE_CHAR
#undef SRE

/* generate 16-bit unicode version */
#define SRE_CHAR Py_UCS2
#define SIZEOF_SRE_CHAR 2
#define SRE(F) sre_ucs2_##F
#include "regex_lib.h"
#undef SRE_CHAR
#undef SIZEOF_SRE_CHAR
#undef SRE

/* generate 32-bit unicode version */
#define SRE_CHAR Py_UCS4
#define SIZEOF_SRE_CHAR 4
#define SRE(F) sre_ucs4_##F
#include "regex_lib.h"
#undef SRE_CHAR
#undef SIZEOF_SRE_CHAR
#undef SRE
```

And call `SRE(match_many_ANY)` instead of `match_many_ANY`.

This is just an example. If use this method, need to convert many functions from top to bottom.

